ne with that is that the  Flynn saga which is at the very heart of  the Trump Russia investigation appears  to have hinged on a trumped-up suspicion  that an incoming not yet in office  administration had broken a  centuries-old law that had never been  prosecuted before when in fact the new  administration's real transgression was  to make it clear it was going to  overturn Barack Obama's policies now the  second incident that I think points to  the dangers of overzealous investigation  is the FBI's use of the Trump dossier I  hope you've all heard of the Trump  dossier  it's the Clinton campaign Oppo research  product the FBI used it as part of its  counterintelligence investigation into  the Trump campaign we know that to  compile the dossier a democratic law  firm hired the opposition research group  fusion GPS who then hired Christopher  Steele that former British spy who paid  a number of Russian collectors he called  them collectors who then talked to other  Russians who provided gossip allegedly  about Trump most spectacular gossip in  that dossier of course was the  description of Trump in a Moscow hotel  room in 2013 watching as prostitutes  carried out a kinky sex scene so Steele  takes this material to the FBI and in a  development that I think is still  astonishing the bureau agrees to pay  Steele to keep doing the work keep  gathering dirt on Trump this is at the  height of the 2016 campaign even though  this deal falls through the FBI still  incorporates the dossier into its Trump  Russian investigation we all know how  they used it to get a wiretap warrant on  Carter page but in the transition one of  the more stunning scenes of the whole  Trump era to  early January 2017 Trump is  president-elect the intelligence Chiefs  James Comey John Brennan Mike Rogers  James clapper they traveled to Trump  Tower to brief the president-elect on  their report about Russian efforts to  interfere with the 2016 campaign which  are real really happened after the  briefing they have devised a plan by  which three of them will leave and James  Comey will stay one-on-one with Trump  and Trump tells once they're alone Trump  tells Comey about the Moscow sex scene  we had earlier earlier had reports that  said Trump told excuse me comb he told  Trump about the whole dossier didn't  happen Comey later said now we just  talked about the hotel thing so he  imagined this the very first time the  incoming president met the FBI director  face-to-face the FBI's message was we  know about you and those hookers in  Russia which is it's kind of astonishing  it's a very j edgar hoover ich there's a  book called russian roulette' authors  are david korn and michael izikoff they  report that Trump immediately felt the  FBI was blackmailing him Trump had seen  this sort of thing before they wrote  certainly is mentor  Roy Cohn knew how this worked so did  commis famous predecessor j edgar Hoover  who quietly let it be known to  politicians that he possessed  information that could destroy their  careers how could Trump think otherwise  when he gets this briefing amazingly  enough the briefing of Trump soon leaks  to the media and it was the fact that  top officials had seen fit to brief the  incoming president about the dossier  that made this a story they legitimized  it and turned it into a story by having  this briefing within hours the website  BuzzFeed published a whole dossier on  the Internet voila it's all out in  public  remember that Charles Schumer the  Democratic leader in the Senate said as  this was happening he said you take on  the intelligence community they have six  ways from Sunday of getting back at you  so with the Logan Act Obama holdovers  used a dead law as a pretense to push  the Trump investigation with the dossier  they used unverified Oppo research not  only to investigate the Trump campaign  but to execute a clever maneuver to make  it all public and this was all done by  the nation's top law enforcement and  intelligence officials targeting a new  president that is troubling and so if  you look at the Clinton foreign  influence campaign and you look at the  Trump foreign influence investigation  you see very very different things you  see sluggish law enforcement in one you  see overzealous law enforcement and the  other you see a largely uninterested  media and one and you see a fixated  media in the other so those are bookends  of political scandal in Washington for  the last twenty years although there are  many many others and I would be happy to  take your questions on any of those or  any other subject you might want to  bring up but thank you very much for  inviting me this evening  you
 

